  "title": "Bluetooth speaker experiment (14 subjects, 6 classes, 31 EEG ch)",
  "description": "A P300-based brain-computer interface dataset for home appliance control, comprising EEG recordings from 14 healthy subjects performing a visual oddball task with 31-channel recordings at 500 Hz sampling rate. The dataset includes 50 training and 30 testing trials per subject, with target and non-target stimulus classifications presented via LCD display in an online BCI paradigm.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were acquired using a 31-channel actiCHamp system (Brain Products) at 500 Hz sampling rate with linked mastoid reference. Participants performed a P300 oddball task with visual flash stimuli presented on an LCD display at 750 ms stimulus onset asynchrony. The standard 10-20 electrode montage was used with active sensors.",
